  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forecast based Anticipatory Action to Strengthen Food Security and Coping Capacity of Households-at-highest risk (WEST)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide multi-purpose cash assistance to communities on the basis of early flood warnings in Bardiya and Kailali. This WFP project provides multi-purpose cash assistance. Additionally, WFP will provide cash top-ups on behalf of UNFPA, to pregnant women to facilitate their referral and transportation to obstetric services and to survivors of gender-based violence to facilitate access to GBV services. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 74,300 people, including 23,000 women, 23,300 men, 31,000 children, and including 1,400 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
